{"bug":"K001","report":"A","v":"partial","ref":"9. Wikilink source ranges omit the final bracket","evidence":"“`[[Wiki]]` produces link start/end ranges `0..7`, although the construct occupies `0..8`.” Identifies the truncated span, but does not identify the end_ix + 1 assignment or end_ix pointing to the closing delimiter’s start."}
{"bug":"K002","report":"A","v":"missed","ref":"10. Empty wikilink aliases render delimiter text","evidence":"“The selected child starts at a closing-bracket node.” This concerns incorrect empty-alias text, not an uncut next chain causing duplicate traversal and exponential event growth."}
{"bug":"K002","report":"B","v":"missed","ref":"10. Wikilink source ranges omit the final bracket","evidence":"“sets the end offset one byte too early.” This concerns truncated source ranges; the report does not identify reused-child next chains, duplicate traversal, or exponential event growth."}
{"bug":"K006","report":"B","v":"found","ref":"1. HTML blocks ignore valid closing tags","evidence":"“uses a case-sensitive search for the opening tag’s corresponding closing tag.” The report cites lowercase <script> with uppercase </SCRIPT> absorbing following Markdown and explicitly states that CommonMark permits case-insensitive closing tags."}
{"bug":"K009","report":"C","v":"missed","ref":"10. CRLF becomes two spaces inside code spans","evidence":"“Each byte is replaced separately, changing code content in ordinary Windows-format documents.” This concerns line-ending normalization, not surrounding-space trimming that removes an all-space code payload."}
